          "kind": "text",
          "value": "In a restaurant, x men and y women are seated on (x + y) chairs at a round table.\nFind the total number of possible ways such that x men are always sitting next to each\nother."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "x!*y!",
        "x!y!"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Treat the x men as one block; arrange this block with y women around a circle in y! ways, then arrange the men inside their block in x! ways."
        }
      ]
